{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>At the mouth of HaShem, by the hand of Moses.</b> With the sons of Kohath and the sons of Merari it is written 'by the hand of Moses.' But with the sons of Gershon it says only 'at the mouth of HaShem.' And if you ask: in the passage above, ״Do not cut off the families of the Kohathites,״ it is written ״and HaShem spoke to Moses and to Aaron״ — therefore it is written here that Moses counted them, and it was said to Moses from the mouth of the Almighty. But with the sons of Merari, where it is not written 'and HaShem spoke,' but only ״the sons of Merari, by their families, etc.,״ it explained at the end of the passage that it was ״at the mouth of HaShem, by the hand of Moses.״ But regarding the sons of Gershon, it is written above ״and HaShem spoke to Moses״ — but Aaron is not mentioned at all; therefore it was not necessary concerning the sons of Gershon to write 'by the hand of Moses.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:55.847136014Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}